Single-database configuration for Flask.

Database migrations (Alembic via Flask-Migrate)
================================================

The schema is now owned by Alembic migrations plus model metadata. In the
`production` profile, Flask does NOT run `db.create_all()`; you must apply
migrations before first boot:

    flask db upgrade

Workflow
--------
  FLASK_APP=run.py
  # development / production
  flask db migrate -m "describe change"   # autogenerate diff from models
  flask db upgrade                        # apply pending migrations
  flask db downgrade <rev>                # roll back when needed
  flask db current                        # revision the DB is on
  flask db heads                          # latest revisions

Baseline
--------
The single revision `12ee9a1299d2` ("full_schema_baseline") is a squashed
baseline capturing the entire current schema (61 tables). It replaces older
partial migrations that only covered a subset of tables. Existing databases
that were previously created with `db.create_all()` are stamped at this
revision (`flask db stamp 12ee9a1299d2`) so future `flask db upgrade` runs
cleanly against them.

Note: for local development convenience the non-production profiles still
auto-create missing tables on boot (`db.create_all()`). Production relies
strictly on migrations.

Indexing / audit
----------------
Audit tables (`audit_logs`) carry indexes on `user_id`, `action` and
`created_at` for fast, uncorrupted append-only history queries.
